From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: utzcoz <utzcoz@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 20:59:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] subprojects/rustix: enable the features an Apple backend
 needs

The Apple branch of the rustix wrap asks for fs, net and pipe. A sys backend
for macOS also needs event for kqueue, mm for mmap, param for the page size,
and shm for anonymous shared memory.

The features are per-target, so nothing else changes.

Reviewed-by: Gurchetan Singh  <gurchetan.singh.foss@gmail.com>
---
 subprojects/packagefiles/rustix-1-rs/meson.build | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/subprojects/packagefiles/rustix-1-rs/meson.build b/subprojects/packagefiles/rustix-1-rs/meson.build
index 42b83a85410..6e799087d21 100644
--- a/subprojects/packagefiles/rustix-1-rs/meson.build
+++ b/subprojects/packagefiles/rustix-1-rs/meson.build
@@ -40,9 +40,13 @@ elif host_machine.system() == 'darwin' or host_machine.system() == 'macos'
   '--cfg', 'feature="use-libc"',
   '--cfg', 'feature="std"',
   '--cfg', 'feature="alloc"',
+  '--cfg', 'feature="event"',
   '--cfg', 'feature="fs"',
+  '--cfg', 'feature="mm"',
   '--cfg', 'feature="net"',
+  '--cfg', 'feature="param"',
   '--cfg', 'feature="pipe"',
+  '--cfg', 'feature="shm"',
   ]
 elif host_machine.system() == 'windows'
   rustix_args += [
